    "result_text": "Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the rule: creating an owner whose lower-cased email already belongs to any other owner is rejected with **409 Conflict**.\n\nTo keep structural impact minimal, I followed the repo's existing pattern of small, single-purpose helper classes (`CityCodes`, `Namesakes`, `Households`, `DailyRegistrations`) rather than expanding the already-complex `addOwner` method:\n\n- **New file** `EmailDuplicates.java` \u2014 a tiny cohesive class (near-zero surrounding complexity) with a case-insensitive `isDuplicate(...)` check, mirroring the sibling helpers' `normalize` idiom.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one guard added (2 lines) alongside the existing telephone-duplicate check, returning `HttpStatus.CONFLICT`.\n\nThe email is compared case-insensitively (the helper normalizes to lower-case, and `Owner.setEmail` already stores lower-cased), so no method or class was grown beyond a minimal guard. The `email-unique` acceptance test and the rest of the suite pass.",
